export const bodyHtml = "\n<p>A gaming desk setup has to handle a large monitor, fast mouse sweeps and a PC or console with plenty of cables. The layouts below fit those needs into the space you actually have.</p>\n<p>Start from the monitor and mouse, then work outward to the PC, lighting and extras.</p>\n<p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> Plan about 30 inches of depth for a 27 inch or larger monitor, and at least 48 inches of width for a single screen plus mouse room. A 34 inch ultrawide is about 31 inches wide (calculated), so allow 55 to 60 inches if you also want speakers and a desk mat.</p>\n<h2 id=\"layouts-by-screen\">Layouts by screen type</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Screen setup</th><th>Panel width, calculated</th><th>Desk width to plan for</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Single 24 inch</td><td>About 21 in</td><td>40 to 48 in</td><td>Good for a small room</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Single 27 inch</td><td>About 23.5 in</td><td>48 to 55 in</td><td>Leaves mouse room</td></tr>\n<tr><td>34 inch ultrawide</td><td>About 31 in</td><td>55 to 60 in</td><td>Centre it on the chair</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Two 27 inch</td><td>About 47 in</td><td>60 to 72 in</td><td>Angle them inward</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p>Panel widths are calculated from the diagonal at standard aspect ratios and ignore bezels and stands. Our <a href=\"/guide/gaming-desk-size-chart\">gaming desk size chart</a> gives fuller dimension guidance, and the <a href=\"/guide/best-gaming-desks\">best gaming desks</a> list models by size.</p>\n<h2 id=\"mouse-and-keyboard-room\">Mouse and keyboard room</h2>\n<p>Low-sensitivity players need a wide mouse sweep, and a compact keyboard buys that room. See the <a href=\"/guide/tkl-vs-full-size-keyboard\">TKL versus full-size comparison</a> and a <a href=\"/guide/best-gaming-desk-pads\">gaming desk pad</a> that covers the whole front area.</p>\n<h2 id=\"pc-and-cables\">Where the PC and cables go</h2>\n<p>Keep the tower off the desk if you can, on the floor with airflow around it or on a shelf. Run display, power and USB through a tray under the desk. The <a href=\"/guide/best-power-strips-for-desks\">desk power strips</a> and <a href=\"/guide/best-under-desk-cable-trays\">cable trays</a> guides cover options.</p>\n<h2 id=\"lighting-and-mood\">Lighting and mood</h2>\n<p>Bias lighting behind the monitor reduces eye strain in a dark room. Keep the brightness low, and avoid colours that reflect on the screen. A <a href=\"/guide/best-monitor-light-bars\">monitor light bar</a> lights the desk instead of the room.</p>\n<h2 id=\"chair-and-posture\">Chair and posture for long sessions</h2>\n<p>Long sessions make chair fit matter more than appearance. Set elbows near 90 degrees and keep the monitor at eye level, the same checks as the <a href=\"/guide/ergonomic-desk-setup\">ergonomic desk setup</a> guide.</p>\n<h2 id=\"faq\">Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>How should I set up a gaming desk?</h3>\n<p>Start with the monitor and mouse, then add the keyboard, lighting, PC and cable routing. Keep the screen's top near eye level.</p>\n<h3>How big a desk do I need for gaming?</h3>\n<p>About 48 inches wide for one monitor, 55 to 60 for an ultrawide, and 60 to 72 for two monitors.</p>\n<h3>How deep should a gaming desk be?</h3>\n<p>About 30 inches suits a large monitor at a comfortable distance, and 24 inches is workable for smaller screens.</p>\n<h3>Where should I put my gaming PC?</h3>\n<p>On the floor with space for airflow, or on a shelf. Avoid enclosed spaces that trap heat.</p>\n<h3>How do I hide cables on a gaming desk?</h3>\n<p>Route them to a power strip and cable tray under the desk and keep a clean front edge.</p>\n<h3>Do I need RGB lighting?</h3>\n<p>No. A light bar or bias light is enough, and it works better with a dimmer.</p>\n<h2 id=\"sources-and-scope\">Sources and scope</h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://www.obsbot.com/blog/work-from-home/ergonomic-desk-setup\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OBSBOT ergonomic desk setup</a>: posture and screen position basics</li><li><a href=\"https://www.csuci.edu/publicsafety/ehs/200320-ci-workstation-setup-checklist.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CSU Channel Islands workstation checklist</a>: keyboard and monitor height advice</li><li><a href=\"https://www.aut.ac.nz/__data/assets/pdf_file/0004/782680/Setting-up-your-workstation-tip-sheet.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">AUT workstation tip sheet</a>: how to place the screen and chair for long sessions</li></ul>\n<p>Desk widths are planning ranges and panel widths are calculated, ignoring bezels and stands. Check dimensions on your actual monitor and desk.</p>";
